\b\cf0\ulc0\insrsid356453 \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1  What is bank overdraft? Mention an example for this. Why companies have to pay mark up on it. Under which head mark up paid on overdraft is shown in financial statement.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf0\ulc0\insrsid14949411 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Answer:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf0\ulc0\insrsid14949411 
\par \hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 Bank Overdraft is the form of loan taken from the bank when the amount is exceeding from specific limit, and bank deduct this overdraft amount when company\hich\f1 \rquote \loch\f1 
s account debited, As this is the type of Loan and so company have to pay mark up as interest on th\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 e\hich\af1\dbch\af31505\loch\f1 
 overdraft amount and depend upon the terms of agreement. In the financial statement the mark up is shown in Financial Expenses.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf0\ulc0\insrsid356453 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf0\ulc0\insrsid356453 
